<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd Allah ibn Ishaq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1203</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a> ibn Ishaq was a ruler of the Banu Ghaniya, the Almoravid family that held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> after the Almoravid collapse in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. While his brothers waged war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a>, he governed the island until an Almohad fleet conquered Majorca in 1203 and he was killed.</p></div>
